    "https://www.clayton.edu/career/index.php": {
      "title": "Career and Professional Development",
      "description": "Career and Professional Development - Clayton State University Skip to Content We use cookies to give you the best experience and to help improve our website. For more information see our Privacy Notice . Questions or requests, please complete our DSR form . Ok Toggle navigation LochNet Directory Giving Apply Search on Desktop Search on mobile About About Home Visit Us History & Traditions Fast Facts Work at CSU Office of the President Administration Community Outreach Contact Us Academics Academics Home Undergraduate Study Degrees, Majors & Certificates Graduate Study Colleges & Schools Academic Affairs Academic Catalog Course Search Course Syllabi Academic Resources Online Learning Faculty Members' Profiles Admissions Admissions Home Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Orientation Continuing Education Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Forms Request Information Student Life Student Life Home Arts & Culture Books & Dining Campus Technology Career and Professional Development Care Center Community, Belonging & Veterans Center Dean of Students Health & Wellness Lakers Care & Share Parents Student Care & Support Student Engagement Transportation & Parking Services University Housing Athletics Alumni Alumni Home Events Get Involved Stay Connected Alumni Benefits Membership Laker Pride Alumni Giving Contact Alumni Career and Professional Development Toggle navigation Students Career Assessment Type Career Development Checklist Career Exploration Career and Professional Development Events Employer Information Session Graduate School Information Internship Information Job Fair Information Job Search Information Laker CareerZone On-Campus Recruiting & Interviewing Presentation Request Form Stepping Blocks Student Worker Guidelines What can I do with my Major? Workshops Employers Career Fair Information Employer Information Sessions Employer Policies Internship Information Job Posting Information On-Campus Recruiting & Interviewing Program and Student Facts Travel Information Alumni & Families Employer Information Session Events Families Graduate School Information Job Fair Information Job Search Information Laker Career Mentoring Program On-Campus Recruiting & Interviewing Career Outcomes Faculty & Staff Alternative to Canceling Class Career Counseling Guidelines for Student Workers Online Career Guide Contact Us While at Clayton State, your job is to explore. To discover your strengths and define\n                     what you want to do with them. To seize opportunities that come your way. Our job\n                     in Career and Professional Development is to help make all of that possible for you. At every stage of your college career, we provide the resources you need for success\n                     both during your time here and in your professional life after graduation. From resume\n                     building and interview guidance to career fairs, internships and career coaching,\n                     there is no shortage of pathways to making your dream real. Let’s get started! Laker CareerZone Utilize this career management system to discover new job, internship, work study\n                                       opportunities and register for workshops/events! Student Login (Upload your résumé and apply for jobs!) Recruiter Login Post jobs and register for events! Resume Review The Office of Career and Professional Development resume reviews are on Tuesdays from\n                                          2–4 p.m. and Wednesdays from 10 a.m.–2 p.m. on Microsoft Teams, or in-person Edgewater\n                                          Hall, Suite 228. Book a Resume Review Session Upcoming Events Sep 8 Resume Review Sep 9 Resume Review Sep 14 Internship Week Kick-Off Sep 15 Resume Review Sep 15 Internship Job Search Strategies Workshop Sep 16 Internship Networking Breakfast Internships Information Internships integrate knowledge and theory learned in the classroom with practical\n                                          application and skills development in a professional setting. Internships give students\n                                          the opportunity to gain valuable applied experience and make connections in professional\n                                          fields they are considering for career paths; and give employers the opportunity to\n                                          guide and evaluate talent. Students Employers Career Exploration Career Decisions Clayton State Majors and Related Careers Interests Personality Skills and Abilities Salary Career Decisions Learn More Steppingblocks Steppingblocks is an online career exploration platform. Students, faculty, and staff\n                                          have access to a 20-question personality assessment, a career path explorer, an institutional\n                                          outcomes explorer, and a tuition analyzer. Learn more about Steppingblocks Online Career Guide This online resource is full of tips, advice and samples regarding career assessments,\n                                       job search strategies, resume and cover letter development, interviewing, social media\n                                       and dressing for success. View the Career Guide Laker Link Career MENTORING PROGRAM Our program directors work with you to make sure that you take the courses you need\n                                       for your degree plan. They’re experts at navigating program-completion requirements\n                                       and can help keep you on track as you work toward graduation. Learn More Career Videos Thousands of videos! Industry professionals sharing their job descriptions, backgrounds\n                                          and preparation advice. “Get Hired” advice videos on interviewing, resume writing,\n                                          and many more topics to help you land that job! Learn More Big Interview Use Big Interview video and virtual tutorial to develop and practice interviewing\n                                          skills with unlimited interview practice sessions. Learn More Professional Clothing Closet The Professional Clothing Closet provides a way for Clayton State University students\n                                       to access FREE professional attire appropriate for career fairs, interviews, and the\n                                       workplace. Inventory includes suits, blazers, skirts, button-down shirts, and more.\n                                       Our goal is to help students look their best throughout their job search so they can\n                                       make a positive impression as they enter the professional world! Clothing Donations: Transform Your Closet Cleaning into Life-Changing Opportunities! Contact us for more\n                                          information on your planned donation. Email Career and Professional Development Corporate Partners View the Corporate Partners Student Spotlight Michelle Roache Learn More Berquila Arnold Learn More Share Your Story prev next Contact Career and Professional Development Location: Edgewater Hall, Suite 228 Phone: (678) 466-5400 Fax: (678) 466-5468 Email: Email Career and Professional Development Office Hours: Monday-Friday, 8 a.m.–5 p.m. Meet the Staff Find Your Major Apply Accreditation Strategic Plan Contact Us Public Safety Visitor Information Parking 2000 Clayton State Boulevard Morrow, GA 30260 (678) 466-4000 Maps & Directions Clayton State University Facebook Clayton State University Twitter Clayton State University Instagram Clayton State University YouTube Clayton State University LinkedIn A-Z index Calendar Laker Newsroom Offices/Depts Employment Title IX Anti-Hazing Accessibility 2000 Clayton State Boulevard Morrow, GA 30260 (678) 466-4000 Clayton State University Facebook Clayton State University Twitter Clayton State University Instagram Clayton State University YouTube Clayton State University LinkedIn © Clayton State University A Senior Unit of the University System of Georgia Ethics & Integrity Human Trafficking Notice Equal Opportunity Privacy ©"
