    "https://gbi.georgia.gov/press-releases/2018-07-02/gbi-announces-2018-human-trafficking-notice-website-posting": {
      "title": "GBI Announces 2018 Human Trafficking Notice Website Posting",
      "description": "GBI Announces 2018 Human Trafficking Notice Website Posting | Georgia Bureau of Investigation Skip to main content An official website of the State of Georgia. How you know Language icon English Organizations The .gov means it’s official. Local, state, and federal government websites often end in .gov. State of Georgia government websites and email systems use “georgia.gov” or “ga.gov” at the end of the address. Before sharing sensitive or personal information, make sure you’re on an official state website. Still not sure? Call 1-800-GEORGIA to verify that a website is an official website of the State of Georgia. Georgia.gov logo Georgia Bureau of Investigation GBI: State of Georgia Bureau of Investigation Constition: wisdom, justice, moderation Georgia Bureau of Investigation Search Close Menu Main navigation About Us Subnavigation toggle for About Us Director Assistant Director Administration Publications Monthly Statistical Report Frequently Asked Questions GBI History GBI Organizational Chart Services Subnavigation toggle for Services Applicant Services BINGO Child Fatality Review Program CJIS Vendor Compliance Program Crime Statistics GAPS - Georgia Applicant Processing Service Georgia Criminal History Record Restrictions Georgia Sex Offender Registry Georgia's Public Alert System Law Enforcement Links Meth Container Program Obtaining Criminal History Record Information Prevent Child Abuse (PCA) Georgia Secondary Metals Recycling Divisions Subnavigation toggle for Divisions Division of Forensic Sciences Georgia Crime Information Center Investigative Division Medical Examiner's Office Employment Subnavigation toggle for Employment GBI Vacancies State of Georgia Vacancies Job Profiles Internship Program Employee Benefits Employment Disqualifiers Employment FAQ ADA Unsolved Cases Subnavigation toggle for Unsolved Cases Unsolved Homicides Unidentified Remains Missing Persons Robberies News Subnavigation toggle for News 2026 Press Releases 2025 Press Releases 2024 Press Releases 2023 Press Releases 2022 Press Releases 2021 Press Releases 2020 Press Releases 2019 Press Releases 2018 Press Releases 2017 Press Releases 2016 Press Releases 2015 Press Releases 2014 Press Releases 2013 Press Releases 2012 Press Releases 2011 Press Releases 2010 Press Releases 2009 Press Releases 2008 Press Releases 2007 Press Releases GBI Payment Portal Subnavigation toggle for GBI Payment Portal GBI Payment Portal FAQs GBI Payment Portal Instructions GBI Payment Portal Security Certificate Contact Us Subnavigation toggle for Contact Us Directions Header Utility Narrow Search this site Enter your keywords Popular searches Mission Statement Organization of the office History Meeting Requests Key Staff Duties of the Office Event Requests Contact Breadcrumb Home News GBI Announces 2018 Human Trafficking Notice Website Posting News 2026 Press Releases Subnavigation toggle for 2026 Press Releases 2026 Officer Involved Shootings 2025 Press Releases Subnavigation toggle for 2025 Press Releases 2025 Officer Involved Shootings 2024 Press Releases Subnavigation toggle for 2024 Press Releases 2024 Officer Involved Shootings 2023 Press Releases Subnavigation toggle for 2023 Press Releases 2023 Officer Involved Shootings 2022 Press Releases Subnavigation toggle for 2022 Press Releases 2022 Officer Involved Shootings 2021 Press Releases Subnavigation toggle for 2021 Press Releases 2021 Officer Involved Shootings 2020 Press Releases Subnavigation toggle for 2020 Press Releases 2020 Officer Involved Shootings 2019 Press Releases 2018 Press Releases 2017 Press Releases 2016 Press Releases 2015 Press Releases 2014 Press Releases 2013 Press Releases 2012 Press Releases 2011 Press Releases 2010 Press Releases 2009 Press Releases 2008 Press Releases 2007 Press Releases July 02, 2018 GBI Announces 2018 Human Trafficking Notice Website Posting Decatur, GA (July 2, 2018) – The Georgia Bureau of Investigation announces the 2018 Human Trafficking Notice posting on its website: https://gbi.georgia.gov/human-trafficking-notice . Per Georgia law (O.C.G.A. § 16-5-47), the following businesses and other establishments are required to post the notice in each public restroom and in a conspicuous place near the public entrance of the business or establishment or where similar notices are customarily posted: 1) Adult entertainment establishments; 2) Bars; 3) Primary airports; 4) Passenger rail or light rail stations; 5) Bus stations; 6) Truck stops; 7) Emergency rooms within general acute care hospitals; 8) Urgent care centers; 9) Farm labor contractors and day haulers; 10) Privately operated job recruitment centers; 11) Safety rest areas located along interstate highways in this state; 12) Hotels; 13) Businesses and establishments that offer massage or bodywork services by a person who is not a massage therapist; and 14) Government buildings Please reference O.C.G.A. § 16-5-47 for full business/establishment definitions and details. Contact Information: Nelly Miles - Public Affairs Director - 404-270-8330 Related Files Human Trafficking Post - revised 070118.pdf (PDF, 35.91 KB) Georgia.gov logo Georgia Bureau of Investigation Facebook page for Georgia Bureau of Investigation X (Twitter) page for Georgia Bureau of Investigation How can we help? Call Us Primary: (404) 244-2600 TTY: (800) 255-0056 Voice: (800) 255-0135 Speech to Speech: (888) 202-4082 Spanish to Spanish: (888) 202-3972 Online Tip Form Submit Tips Online Visit 3121 Panthersville Road Decatur, GA 30034 US About Us Careers FAQ © Georgia.gov Accessibility Privacy/Security Website powered by GovHub Human Trafficking Notice Georgia Web Analytics"
    }
